# Deterministic Engineering Guidelines

## Core Invariants
- Enforce strict typing across all interfaces and data structures.
- Validate external boundaries immediately with declarative schemas before business logic execution.
- Ensure all asynchronous calls specify explicit timeouts and unhandled rejection catches.
- Prefer deterministic mathematical algorithms and constant-time comparisons for security-critical logic.
- Emit structured RFC-7807 problem payloads on failure:
  `{ "type": "https://errors.example.com/invalid-input", "title": "Validation Error", "status": 400, "detail": "Field amount must be positive" }`